Revolution","u":"4","desc":"This five-week global seminar in Edinburgh will examine the core philosophical, scientific, political, and cultural ideas that formed the basis of the Enlightenment, the romantic movement, and revolutions in Europe and America from the late seventeenth century through the first half of the nineteenth century. Revelle students must take course for letter grade. Students may receive credit for one of the following: HUM 4, HUM 4R, or HUM 4GS.","pre":"satisfaction of the UC Entry Level Writing requirement and acceptance into Global Seminar Program.","unl":[],"hist":[],"ge":[],"gpa":null,"aRate":null,"terms":0,"offered":0,"seatUrl":null,"tss":null,"res":null,"fa":[],"profs":[],"sec":[]},"HUM 4R":{"t":"Enlightenment, Romanticism, Revolution","u":"4","desc":"The Enlightenment’s revisions of traditional thought; the rise of classical liberalism; the era of the first modern political revolutions; Romantic ideas of nature and human life. This course is a distance education course. Revelle students must take course for letter grade. Students may receive credit for one of the following: HUM 4, HUM 4R, or HUM 4GS.","pre":"satisfaction of the UC Entry Level Writing requirement; open to Revelle students only.","unl":[],"hist":[],"ge":[],"gpa":null,"aRate":null,"terms":0,"offered":0,"seatUrl":null,"tss":null,"res":null,"fa":[],"profs":[],"sec":[]},"HUM 5":{"t":"Modern Culture (1848–present)","u":"4","desc":"Through the study of selected core texts, this course explores challenges to the Western tradition of cultural and political thought brought about by the significant social, political, and cultural changes since the late nineteenth century, such as the world wars, decolonization, technological innovations, and globalization. Revelle students must take course for letter grade. Students may receive credit for one of the following: HUM 5, HUM 5R, or HUM 5GS.","pre":"satisfaction of the UC Entry Level Writing requirement; open to Revelle students only.","